# Netlify SPA fallback (operations-and-deployment-readiness 1.1/1.2).
#
# Semantics: existing static files are served first; MISSING files fall
# through these rules in order. Asset classes are routed to the honest 404
# page with a 404 status (a missing asset must never masquerade as the app
# shell); everything else is a client-side route and receives index.html
# WITH THE ORIGINAL URL PRESERVED (the SPA router reads location.pathname).
#
# Sub-path hosting: use a `base`-configured build and rewrite with the
# sub-path prefix (docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §sub-path).
/*.js    /404.html  404
/*.css   /404.html  404
/*.map   /404.html  404
/*.json  /404.html  404
/*.wasm  /404.html  404
/*.png   /404.html  404
/*.jpg   /404.html  404
/*.svg   /404.html  404
/*.bin   /404.html  404
/*       /index.html  200
